codex
One final gate audit exposed a subtle G4 issue: the displayed magnitudes make it freely deducible that a valid answer has exactly one target-scale denominator and ten large denominators. Uniform sampling over all eleven-subsets was therefore too naive. I’m tightening `CERTIFICATE_LANGUAGE`, `random_candidate`, `search_space`, and the meet-in-the-middle baseline to enforce that obvious constraint; the resulting shipping prior is still billions of candidates, but it is the honest one.
apply patch
