 ## Caveats
 
-The exact density is with respect to uniform eleven-subsets of the displayed list; it says nothing about a solver using the common-scale prior.  The five normalized answers are deliberately all present at non-demo presets, so memorizing the five `k=9` identities makes the compact route easier.  Plants satisfy a correlation that independent decoys do not—the reciprocal identity itself—although planted and decoy tails share the same odd scaled form and multiplier range.  I did not test lattice reduction, a general-purpose CP/SAT encoding, or vendor models because the required oracle pool was quota-blocked.  Most importantly, local attacks are not a substitute for STEP 4: this family remains provisional until the four-vendor bare run says `hardened`.
+The exact density is with respect to uniform eleven-subsets of the displayed list; it says nothing about a solver using the paper's block prior. Indeed, recognizing `q+2d` makes the family easy by design, and a solver that has memorized the five `k=9` identities has an additional shortcut. Every candidate comes from a complete valid block, eliminating a planted-versus-decoy marginal signature, but this introduces correlations that a stronger gcd/divisibility clusterer could exploit. I did not test lattice reduction, a general-purpose CP/SAT encoding, or a full pairwise-gcd clustering panel. No vendor model produced a valid attempt because the required OpenRouter key was quota-blocked. Most importantly, local attacks are not a substitute for STEP 4: this family remains provisional until the four-vendor bare run says `hardened`.
