codex
Implemented the verified Track B generator based on Lemma 2.5(a) of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1606.02117v1).

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1606.02117/gen_1606_02117.py:34)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1606.02117/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1606.02117/README.md:1)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1606.02117/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1606.02117/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1606.02117/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates all pass:

- Exactly 4 valid witnesses among 3,390,642,112 structure-aware candidates.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five attacks: all 0/8.
- Reference meet-in-the-middle: 8/8, averaging 7,103,905 modular additions.
- Intended structural route: 8/8 in at most 153 exact operations.
- Answer: 561 characters worst case, 11 elements.

STEP 4 remains externally blocked. Every bare, hinted, and placebo request received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “key total limit exceeded”; therefore there are zero valid oracle attempts and no honest `hardened` verdict. The README and script-generated transcripts record this explicitly, and submission correctly remains blocked pending restored quota.
